  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Survey Field Book",
    "overview": "GEE-Assist is one PyQt6 desktop app with one shared design system (three live themes, one solid theme-reactive button accent, one button radius, three bundled faces) and three layouts built on it. Layout 1 (classical) and Layout 2 (modern, map-first) are structural variants of the shared base. Layout 3 (\"studio\") is a visual world of its own laid over that base: the analyst's field book. Every page is a ruled, indexed spread under a graphite cover with a yellow spine.\n\nThe field book lends exactly four things to the shared base, and only these: palette (graphite cover, field-book yellow, one hue per division), type (every figure in one measurement mono), density (24px page margins, ruled tables, the run log open), and the ruled 8px module drawn on the page ground. It never moves controls or changes what a page does. Result maps are the only full colour on the page; charts are drawn in yellow and muted ink.\n\nLayout 3 is the power workspace and is dark-first: the dark blue-green and dark grey themes lead, and the light theme must hold. Depth is tonal and ruled, never lifted.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Graphite cover nav, darker than the page in every theme, with a 6px field-book-yellow spine on its right edge.",
      "Index numbers (Alt+1 to Alt+0, in page order) drawn in yellow mono where the nav icons would be.",
      "Four divisions (Work, Analyse, Explain, Report), each with one fixed hue: on the cover headings and on the checked division tab.",
      "Page ground ruled on an 8px hairline tile; flat sheets with 1px rules and a 6px corner.",
      "Yellow 1px rules under table headers, current-project rows and the spread's gutter.",
      "Every figure (counts, values, timings, paths, entry numbers) in JetBrains Mono.",
      "One solid button accent per theme, 10px radius, shared by all three layouts."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Yellow Rule",
        "body": "Field-book yellow is the only accent the field book adds. It rules, it numbers, it marks progress; it is never a button fill and never a large area.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Maps Are The Colour Rule",
        "body": "In Layout 3 the result maps are the only full-colour surfaces. Charts use yellow and muted ink; division hues appear only on headings and the checked tab.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Accent Rule",
        "body": "Every primary button in every layout is the active theme's solid accent. Layouts differ in structure and surfaces, never in button hue.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Measurement Face Rule",
        "body": "In Layout 3 every figure is JetBrains Mono. A number set in Inter is a defect.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Ruled Not Lifted Rule",
        "body": "Field-book sheets never cast shadows. Separation is a 1px border or a yellow rule.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Half-Height Rule",
        "body": "Qt ignores a border-radius larger than half a widget's height and draws square corners instead. Buttons keep `BUTTON_RADIUS` (10px); never raise it.",
        "section": "shapes"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** build every theme-dependent stylesheet through `theming.styled(widget, builder)`, with a builder that reads current theme values, so it recolours live. Painter-drawn widgets read `theme.*` at paint time; subscribe anything else with `theming.on_theme_changed`.",
      "**Do** expect a theme change to apply live and a layout change to restart the app; read `fieldbook.active()` once.",
      "**Do** keep every button at `BUTTON_RADIUS` (10px) and every primary button on the theme's solid accent.",
      "**Do** set every figure in JetBrains Mono in Layout 3.",
      "**Do** mark division with the division strip and the side index, and number entries in yellow.",
      "**Do** use the ink variants of division hues on the light theme, and pencil-dark yellow (yellow-ink-light) where yellow is text on a light page.",
      "**Do** check every new Layout 3 surface in all three themes, dark first."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** raise a button radius above half its height: Qt draws square corners instead.",
      "**Don't** rely on a QLabel bottom border to mark a page title or section: it does not paint reliably. Use the division strip and the side index, or a QFrame rule.",
      "**Don't** set a stylesheet with a one-off `setStyleSheet(f\"...\")` that reads theme colours: it freezes on the theme it was built in.",
      "**Don't** add shadows to Layout 3 sheets or cards.",
      "**Don't** fill buttons or large areas with field-book yellow, and don't give charts or chrome full colour in Layout 3: result maps carry the colour.",
      "**Don't** use a division hue outside its own division's heading and tab.",
      "**Don't** set figures in Inter or the display face in Layout 3."
    ]
  }
}